{"title":"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph shows the nutritional contents of a Pascal Burger. Which ratio compares the mass of fats to the mass of carbohydrates?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c746e240142cbc406270f68eaaa66fd9dafbbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3:2 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2:3 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 2:1 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4:3 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 3:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"509\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the bar graph, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grams of fats and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grams of carbohydrates in a Pascal Burger. The ratio of the mass of fats to the mass of carbohydrates in a Pascal Burger would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f9ccd2f559c3c97c636ba90930115446ad2423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32:48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The greatest common divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so we can divide both by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to get the reduced form.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f9ccd2f559c3c97c636ba90930115446ad2423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32:48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/62300f521712cdab14ce443c38c95eae954a8c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"81\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal\">2011 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEM